== Research
I am a mineral physicist interested in planetary materials. I am drawn to this field because here the very small and the very large are bound together: what happens among atoms and electrons decides how planets form and evolve. My group recreates the extreme pressures and temperatures of planetary interiors through synchrotron experiments, atomistic simulations, and thermodynamic models. These tools let us connect the physics and chemistry of materials to what we observe of Earth and of other worlds we may never visit, and yet may come to know.

Themes of our current projects:

- Thermodynamics of planetary materials
- Volatiles and the habitability of rocky planets
- Interiors of giant planets and exoplanets

